<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[{!Contact.FirstName},<br><br>Greetings. It is my pleasure to inform you that after careful evaluation of our applicants, we are pleased to recommend your admission to the Master of Arts in Social Justice and Human Rights at Arizona State University. Although you should consider this notice an unofficial acceptance (to be followed by official acceptance via email from the ASU Graduate College), please accept my hearty congratulations on behalf of the Graduate Studies Admissions Committee.<br><br>As Director of the M.A. in Social Justice and Human Rights, I welcome you to our program. Prior to the start of the semester we have scheduled a mandatory orientation meeting. At this meeting I will provide information to help you as you begin the process of earning you M.A. In addition, you will be able to meet your fellow entering students and ask questions about the program.<br><br>You will find answers to many questions in the <a href="https://newcollege.asu.edu/sites/default/files/files/advising/documents/sjhr_graduate_handbook_2015-2016.pdf">program handbook</a>. If you have questions related to tuition, financial aid or housing, please view the <a href="https://newcollege.asu.edu/graduate/admission-next-steps">next steps</a> section for a number of University Offices available to assist you. If you have questions related to the program or registration, please contact the Academic Success Coordinator, Jan Lacey at ncgradadvising@asu.edu.<br><br>In the meantime, congratulations! I look forward to meeting you at our orientation and please <a href="https://newcollege.asu.edu/graduate/admission-next-steps">click here for your next steps</a>.<br><br>Please follow <a href="https://newcollege.asu.edu/graduate/acceptance-form">this link</a> to complete a form to either accept or decline our offer of admission.<br><br>Julie Murphy Erfani, PhD<br>Associate Professor &amp; Director of MA Social Justice and Human Rights Program<br>School of Social and Behavioral Sciences<br>Phone: 602-543-6015<br><a href="mailto:julie.murphy.erfani@asu.edu">Julie.Murphy.Erfani@asu.edu</a><br><font color="#C0C0C0"><br><font size="1">{!Case.Thread_Id}</font></font><br>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>